 Basic 
Services to be provided by Consultant hereunder shall consist of performing all of those 
activities necessary or appropriate for Consultant to perform as the MERF's primary
investment advisor for its investment program as contemplated by the Policy Statement. 
These services shall include, but not necessarily be limited to:
2.1 Policy Duties:
(i) Annually, review the Investment Policy Statements ("IPS")
(ii) Recommend and assist in drafting changes to the IPS;
(iii) Assist in establishing and/or revising asset class level manager guidelines and
restrictions;
(iv) Annually, review and recommend appropriate benchmark revisions;
(v) Annually, provide capital market assumptions and expected returns to model asset 
allocation updates;
(vi) Assist in establishing systems and procedures for monitoring policies on an 
ongoing basis;
(vii) Provide recommendations concerning long-term investment policy, investment
objectives and strategy, including manager continuation policies and rebalancing 
policies;
(viii) Provide recommendations concerning investment goals, policies, guidelines and 
procedures for private and publicly managed portfolios;
(ix) Provide recommendations concerning risk management policies, and other related 
issues; 
(x) Provide compliance monitoring.
2.2 Asset Allocation & Total Portfolio Duties:
(i) Conduct periodic asset allocation and asset-liability studies; 
(ii) Conduct annual asset allocation reviews and provide corresponding asset allocation
recommendations addressing relevant risk and return parameters; 
(iii) Provide asset class research, analysis, and recommendations;

